      "assistant_text": "The index update seems to have a constraint I\u0027m not meeting. However, I\u0027ve successfully created the Synthesis Page. Let me answer your question directly based on what I\u0027ve found:\n\n## The Connection\n\nYour credential-scoping and runtime-path decisions are **two instances of the same architectural principle**: both centralize configuration at a single startup composition point, resolving everything once upfront and then treating those resolved values as immutable constants downstream.\n\n**Credential Scoping** ([[credential-scoping]]) implements this for secrets: the Hub reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into each child process\u0027s environment. The Hub\u0027s own process environment never holds the key, preventing accidental leaks.\n\n**Runtime Paths** ([[runtime-paths]]) implements this for file locations: every path the Hub touches \u2014 wiki root, database, secrets file, agent instruction directories \u2014 is resolved in exactly one place at startup through a single path resolver. Configuration is read once (command line, environment variables, config file, or defaults), validated, and then every other part of the codebase consumes the already-resolved paths rather than rediscovering them.\n\nThe shared value is **immutability and composability**: once decided at startup, both the credential set and the path set are constants. No agent or subsystem re-evaluates or mutates them. This eliminates injection vulnerabilities because there is no \u0022wrong key\u0022 or \u0022wrong path\u0022 branch in your downstream code \u2014 the Hub has already composed everything, and each component receives its pre-decided environment.\n\nI\u0027ve saved this connection as a new page, [[concepts/single-composition-point]], which synthesizes both pages to make the relationship explicit.",
